42. DO NOT FAKE COMPLETENESS

If the literature does not permit reconstruction of a historical step with confidence:

do not invent it.

Mark it:

Reconstruction uncertain

and explain the assumption.

If a popular historical claim cannot be supported:

exclude it.

This application will be more impressive if it is demonstrably trustworthy.

